# Normalize line endings for everything git treats as text, on both
# checkin and checkout, regardless of any given clone's core.autocrlf.
# Mirrors .editorconfig's `end_of_line = lf` / CLAUDE.md's "LF endings"
# convention. This is what actually stops the CRLF/LF fight -- without it,
# a Windows editor (VS, a Lua/PS1 editor set to CRLF) resaving a file with
# CRLF makes every future diff a full-file rewrite instead of the real
# change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary -- never touch, never diff as text.
*.ico -text
*.png -text
*.exe -text
*.dll -text
*.zip -text
